**Interpretation.** Tuned to a triage-appropriate 85% sensitivity, the full model flags roughly half of the external population (pre 51%, post 56%) at a PPV of 0.142 (pre) and 0.187 (post), i.e. a number needed to screen of 7.1 and 5.4. The 5-item deployment model is close behind (PPV 0.122 and 0.170; NNS 8.2 and 5.9), as is the 7-item variant (NNS 7.3 and 5.4). After local recalibration, net benefit is positive and exceeds both default strategies at threshold probabilities of 0.10?0.15 in every dataset and for every model size, supporting use as a low-burden digital triage aid rather than a diagnostic test.

