# Multimedia Appendix 4. Transportability-ceiling analyses

Supporting Results Ёз3.5 (concept-shift ceiling) and Discussion Ёз4.4 (development-survey coverage). All model selection used KCHS-internal criteria only. NHANES labels are used throughout for evaluation, as in any external validation; what is quarantined to the oracle rows is their use for model *fitting* (a deliberate Ёз2.10 violation, for diagnosis only). Weighted AUROC throughout.

## Table S2a. Leakage-controlled attempts to exceed the external ceiling

Every learner and adaptation was trained on KCHS and applied to NHANES without refitting (unless noted). None exceeded the pre-specified LightGBM baseline once selection was restricted to KCHS-internal information.

| Strategy | External pre | External post | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| **LightGBM baseline (17 predictors, primary)** | **0.772** | **0.769** | reference |
| Add public-assistance receipt (welfare) | 0.772 | 0.769 | no change |
| Add welfare + 12-mo welfare | 0.772 | 0.769 | no change |
| Add welfare + weekend sleep | 0.771 | 0.769 | no change |
| Increase KCHS training 0.5M Ёц 1.0M | 0.768 | 0.768 | lower |
| Increase KCHS training 0.5M Ёц 2.0M | 0.767 | 0.767 | lower |
| 5-seed probability ensemble | 0.769 | 0.768 | ? |
| Logistic-regression transfer | 0.759 | 0.760 | lower |
| Elastic-net transfer | 0.759 | 0.760 | lower |
| LightGBM + logistic blend (w=0.5) | 0.768 | 0.771 | offsetting |
| Covariate-shift density-ratio reweighting | 0.766 | 0.758 | lower |
| Within-survey quantile normalization | 0.762 | 0.773 | offsetting |

Two adaptations moved pre and post in opposite directions (blend, quantile normalization); neither yields a net gain selectable without external labels.

## Table S2a-2. Prespecified method search (independent re-run, 300k KCHS training)

An additional seven leakage-free strategies were run with an in-run same-sample baseline (pre 0.769, post 0.769). None improved both external cohorts. Notably, a leave-one-year-out (LOYO) transfer-robustness search re-selected the primary hyperparameters, and a transport-stability feature search retained all predictors?independent confirmations that the deployed model is already well specified. Maximizing internal cross-validation (M7) raised pre but lowered post, illustrating that internal optimization does not transfer consistently.

| Method | External pre | External post | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| Baseline (300k) | 0.769 | 0.769 | reference |
| Monotonic constraints (clinical direction) | 0.761 | 0.746 | lower |
| Transport-stable feature selection (PSI; internal-selected k=0) | 0.769 | 0.769 | no change |
| LOYO transfer-robust hyperparameters (re-selected baseline) | 0.769 | 0.769 | no change |
| KCHS per-year model ensemble | 0.765 | 0.766 | lower |
| Out-of-fold weight-of-evidence target encoding | 0.769 | 0.770 | no change |
| Missing-indicator augmentation | 0.768 | 0.769 | no change |
| Explicit imputation (no tree-native missing) | 0.769 | 0.768 | no change |
| Internal-CV-tuned configuration | 0.772 | 0.767 | offsetting (preЁш, postЁщ) |

