docs\appendix2_crosswalk.md:104:Deviations from the locked document and the parent protocol are reported here and, rule by rule, in Multimedia Appendix 3 Table S11. They comprise: the post-hoc candidate screening described below; a parsimony margin reported at both the planned 0.02 and a stricter 0.01; an alcohol variable operationalized as current drinking alone rather than current plus at-risk drinking; the planned BMI self-report-versus-measured comparison, prior-diagnosis exclusion and alternative physical-activity definition, none of which the data support; the planned R components, which were not used; and public registration, which was not completed. After the primary analysis was complete, the remaining harmonizable-but-unused items (public-assistance receipt, alcohol frequency and quantity, binge drinking, weekend sleep duration) were screened by comparing the direction of their adjusted associations with depression across the three cohorts. This screening inspected NHANES outcome associations and so lies outside the locked plan; it is reported in Methods §2.5.1 as a post-hoc diagnostic. It did not change the predictor set: no item was added, because those with a consistent direction added no external discrimination (ΔAUROC <0.001) and the remainder reversed direction between countries.
