66:All missing-data handling was performed by a preprocessing pipeline fitted in the development training set and applied unchanged to the internal hold-out and to each external set (no leakage). In the gradient-boosting primary model, binary predictors were passed through with missingness preserved and handled natively by the tree learnerâ€”so structurally missing binary items such as living-alone in NHANES pre are never imputed to a constantâ€”while continuous predictors were median-imputed and categorical predictors mode-imputed within the same pipeline. For the linear comparator, continuous predictors were median-imputed, categorical predictors mode-imputed, and binary predictors mode-imputed with an added missing indicator. Household income (within-survey quintile), self-rated health and self-rated oral health are ordinal scores and were modeled as numeric variables rather than as unordered categories, so they were median-imputed and standardized. Alternative strategies (missing indicators added for continuous and binary predictors; single chained-equations imputation of the continuous predictors) were examined in sensitivity analysis (Â§2.12). A silent-column-omission check was added after a data-integrity audit (see Â§2.13).
