..\docs\protocol_text.md:8:Methods. Penalized logistic regression, random forest, and gradient-boosting models will be developed in KCHS using a harmonized predictor set shared with NHANES and evaluated for discrimination, calibration, and clinical utility (decision curve analysis), with SHAP-based interpretation and subgroup fairness. Geographic external validation will be performed in NHANES; temporal validation will contrast the NCHS-defined pre-pandemic (2017–March 2020) and pandemic/post-pandemic (August 2021–August 2023) cycles, with recalibration assessed. A parsimonious model will be derived for digital deployment.
..\docs\protocol_text.md:109:Perceived stress (스트레스 인지)
..\docs\protocol_text.md:137:SHAP values summarize global and local predictor contributions, and the rank concordance of top predictors between KCHS and NHANES is examined as a mechanistic view of transportability. Fairness is assessed by reporting AUROC, calibration, and error rates across sex, age, education, income, and (in NHANES) race/ethnicity. For deployment, a parsimonious model using the top 5–10 predictors is derived to minimize item burden in a self-administered web/mobile form; a conceptual triage workflow routes low-risk users to self-management resources and higher-risk users to professional assessment. The tool is positioned as a screening/triage aid, not a standalone diagnostic or clinical-decision system.
..\docs\protocol_text.md:224:Global SHAP importance and top-predictor rank concordance between surveys are reported (Figure 4). Subgroup discrimination/calibration/error rates by sex, age, education, income, and race/ethnicity are tabulated to characterize equity of performance.
..\docs\protocol_text.md:257:Lundberg SM, Lee S-I. A unified approach to interpreting model predictions (SHAP). Adv Neural Inf Process Syst. 2017;30.
