docs/appendix3_utility.md:204:Other pre-specified rules and their disposition: the parsimony margin follows the plan's recommended 0.02, giving a 5-item deployment model; a stricter 0.01 margin giving 7 items is reported as a post hoc, externally informed variant (§3.6). The operating point is reported both at the recommended sensitivity ≥0.85 and at the alternative Youden point (Tables S1 and S4). Unweighted training with weighted evaluation was used as the primary approach with weighted training as sensitivity, as recommended. The alcohol predictor was specified in the protocol as current drinking **plus at-risk drinking**, but the harmonized variable uses current drinking alone because the NHANES quantity item was not carried through harmonization; three alternative alcohol definitions are reported in Table S7 and change external discrimination by ≤0.003. The planned self-reported-versus-measured BMI comparison and the prior-depression-diagnosis exclusion could not be run because KCHS records only self-reported BMI and no prior diagnosis (§4.4). An alternative physical-activity definition was not available in the harmonized data, which carries only the binary aerobic-recommendation indicator, and income exists only as a within-survey quintile. The four interaction terms evaluated in the feature-representation search were specified when that search was written, not in any earlier dated document. The planned R components were not used — all analyses ran in Python (§2.12).
