docs/cover_letter.md:13:**Methodological rigor and transparency.** The work follows TRIPOD+AI (2024; checklist enclosed as Multimedia Appendix 1) with PROBAST risk-of-bias self-assessment. We report a predictor-set amendment (14→17 predictors) that was documented and locked before any 17-predictor model was fitted — though after the 14-predictor external result was known, which we state explicitly — with the added predictors chosen on survey availability and non-circularity rather than on any outcome association; all model fitting, tuning, algorithm selection, and the choice of deployment item count used development-data cross-validation only, and the 14-predictor comparator was given its own hyperparameter search so the comparison is not confounded by tuning effort. We also disclose and correct three silent data-processing defects found in an adversarial data-integrity audit. The analysis code, variable-harmonization dictionary, model card, and protocol/pre-specification documents will be deposited in a public repository on acceptance; generative AI tools assisted with code and drafting under full author verification.

