I found 32 concrete defects.

## 1. Numeric fidelity — defects found

1. **KCHS sleep missingness is rounded incorrectly.**  
   Quote, MM3 Table S6: “Sleep hours … `11.2% / 0.8% / 1.0%`.”  
   Contradiction: `characteristics_availablecase.csv` records KCHS missingness as 11.25%; direct recomputation gives 11.254375%. Round-half-up to 1 decimal is **11.3%**.  
   Severity: **minor**.  
   Correction: replace 11.2% with 11.3%.

2. **NHANES-post oral-health missingness is rounded incorrectly.**  
   Quote, MM3 Table S6: “Oral health … `0.0% / 0.1% / 0.1%`.”  
   Contradiction: direct recomputation gives post-cycle missingness 0.153551%, which rounds half-up to **0.2%**.  
   Severity: **minor**.  
   Correction: change the post value to 0.2%.

3. **Post-pandemic flag rate is rounded inconsistently.**  
   Quote, manuscript §3.9: “pre 51%, post 55%.”  
   Contradiction: `table_s4_operating.csv` gives `flag rate=0.555`; round-half-up to an integer percentage is **56%**. MM3 already reports 56%.  
   Severity: **minor**.  
   Correction: change 55% to 56%.

4. **“Agreement within 1%” is numerically false.**  
   Quote, manuscript §2.9: “bootstrap 0.00466 vs design 0.00471 … agreement within 1%.”  
   Contradiction: `bootstrap_validation.csv` gives those values; their relative difference is **1.06%** using the design SE as denominator.  
   Severity: **minor**.  
   Correction: report “within approximately 1.1%,” or report only the stored ratio 0.99 without asserting a ≤1% bound.

## 2. Methods versus code — defects found

5. **The KCHS bootstrap merges unrelated singleton PSUs.**  
   Quote, manuscript §2.9: “Strata left with a single primary sampling unit are pooled into one pseudo-stratum.”  
   Contradiction: `54_review3_ci.py:43` replaces every singleton stratum with the same `"__SINGLETON_POOL__"` label and subsequently identifies clusters as `stratum|PSU`. Reused PSU codes therefore merge unrelated original singleton clusters. Of 17,085 singleton year-strata, only 5,956 distinct PSU labels remain: **11,129 clusters are collapsed**. Total KCHS clusters fall from 78,626 to 67,497. Repeating the 1000-replicate calculation while preserving original cluster identity changes the internal CIs to:

   - AUROC: **0.822–0.841**, not 0.823–0.841.
   - AUPRC: **0.215–0.251**, not 0.216–0.254.

   All KCHS subgroup intervals produced by the same class are also affected.  
   Severity: **blocking**.  
   Correction: retain an immutable original `year|stratum|PSU` cluster ID before pooling, rerun all KCHS cohort and domain intervals, and update the manuscript, MM3, model card, ledger, and Figure 6.

6. **The PSU-overlap analysis ignores survey year.**  
   Quote, manuscript §4.4: “92.0% of its records belong to primary sampling units also represented in the training set.”  
   Contradiction: `47_review2_recompute.py` constructs the overlap key from `strata|PSU`, although §2.9 says KCHS strata must be crossed with year because codes recur. `review2_overlap.csv` consequently reports 78,239 hold-out clusters and 72,018 shared clusters. With `year|strata|PSU`, the values are **78,626 clusters, 72,284 shared (91.9%) and 91,846 shared records (91.8%)**.  
   Severity: **important**.  
   Correction: recompute with the year-aware key and replace 92.0% with 91.8%.

7. **MM2 reports raw reused design codes as if they were the analytic KCHS design.**  
   Quote, MM2 Table A3: “5,729 strata; 197,117 stratum–PSU combinations.”  
   Contradiction: these are raw code combinations without year. The stated analytic design has **50,537 year-strata and 199,546 year-stratum–PSU combinations**.  
   Severity: **important**.  
   Correction: label 5,729/197,117 as reused raw codes and report 50,537/199,546 for the analytic design.

8. **Income preprocessing is refitted separately in every external cohort.**  
   Quote, locked prespecification §4: “전처리: 개발셋에서만 학습 → 외부에 그대로 적용” (“Fit preprocessing only in development and apply it unchanged externally”).  
   Contradiction: `../src/01_harmonize.py:78,168` calls `pd.qcut(...,5)` independently in KCHS and each NHANES cycle. External covariate distributions therefore determine the income cut points.  
   Severity: **important**.  
   Correction: either freeze a development-defined transformation or disclose cohort-relative income quintiles as a deviation and specify how an individual deployment population obtains the reference quantiles.

9. **The designated parsimony script implements the post-hoc margin, not the stated primary margin.**  
   Quote, manuscript §2.11: “The item count follows … the smallest set within 0.02 AUROC.”  
   Contradiction: `48_parsimonious_clean.py:79-81` hard-codes `full_sel-0.01` and announces the corresponding seven-item `k*`.  
   Severity: **important**.  
   Correction: make 0.02/k=5 the primary selection executed by the script; run 0.01/k=7 as a separately labelled exploratory branch.

10. **The alcohol sensitivity analysis is misdefined and mistyped.**  
    Quote, MM3 Table S7: “Alcohol redefined as annual drinking frequency.”  
    Contradiction: `../src/15_ext_harmonize.py:15-17,174-176` defines `alcohol_freq` as the **binary indicator of drinking at least twice weekly**. `51_sap_compliance.py:79` nevertheless labels it annual frequency and places it among continuous variables.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: relabel it as binary ≥2 times/week, move it to the binary feature list, rerun the sensitivity analysis, and update Table S7.

11. **Missing drinking frequency is coded as non-drinking.**  
    Quote, manuscript Table 1: “Current drinker.”  
    Contradiction: `../src/01_harmonize.py:83,181` assigns 0 whenever the ever-drinking item is nonmissing, even if frequency is missing/refused. In the external analytic data this misclassifies **4 pre-pandemic participants (weighted 0.040%) and 5 post-pandemic participants (0.062%)**.  
    Severity: **minor**.  
    Correction: assign 0 only for a known non-drinker or valid zero-frequency response; otherwise retain missing and regenerate dependent results.

## 3. Prespecification fidelity — defects found

12. **MM2 overstates outcome blindness.**  
    Quote, MM2 §B.2: “no NHANES outcome data were consulted.”  
    Contradiction: locked prespecification §5 explicitly records the already observed external result, “외부 ~0.75 불변,” and manuscript §2.5.1 acknowledges that the 14-predictor external performance was known.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: say that no *candidate-specific* NHANES outcome association was estimated before locking, while the aggregate 14-predictor external performance was already known.

13. **Post-hoc external-outcome screening is described as not being selection despite determining candidate disposition.**  
    Quote, manuscript §2.5.1: “comparing … adjusted odds ratios … across KCHS, NHANES-pre, and NHANES-post, and then testing them in the model … was not used for selection.”  
    Contradiction: direction reversals and external ΔAUROC were explicitly used to decide that public assistance, alcohol, binge drinking, and weekend sleep would not be retained.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: state that these exploratory candidate dispositions were externally outcome-informed and quarantine them from leakage-controlled selection/ceiling claims.

14. **The 85% sensitivity thresholds use each external cohort’s labels.**  
    Quote, manuscript §3.9: “Tuned to a triage-appropriate 85% sensitivity.”  
    Contradiction: `36_utility.py:61` calls `sens_at(yv,p,w,target)` separately within each evaluation cohort; selection and evaluation use the same cohort outcomes. SAP §9 requires the operating point to be chosen after calibration in the development data.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: choose the primary threshold in development and apply it unchanged externally. Retain current external thresholds only as apparent, cohort-label-informed operating points.

15. **Required repeated cross-validation was not performed or logged as a deviation.**  
    Quote, SAP §7/D5: “5-fold × 5회 반복” (“5-fold × 5 repeats”).  
    Contradiction: the feature search uses one 4-fold run and the equal-protocol audit uses a single 5-fold split; no five-repeat result exists in the authoritative files or Table S11.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: run the prescribed repeated CV or add an explicit deviation with its effect on selection uncertainty.

16. **Local SHAP was required but is absent.**  
    Quote, protocol §2.11: “SHAP values summarize global and local predictor contributions”; SAP §13: “전역/지역 기여도.”  
    Contradiction: only `shap_importance_train.csv` and `shap_cross.csv` contain global summaries; no local explanation analysis or deviation is reported.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: deliver local SHAP results or record the omission as a deviation.

17. **The prespecified fairness scope is incomplete.**  
    Quote, protocol §2.11/SAP §13: fairness includes “AUROC, calibration, and error rates across sex, age, education, income, and … race/ethnicity.”  
    Contradiction: `review3_fairness_domain.csv` covers KCHS sex/age/education and NHANES race, but contains no income-domain analysis and no subgroup error rates. Table S11 does not disclose this omission.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: supply income and error-rate analyses or log each omission as a deviation.

18. **The planned pregnancy sensitivity analysis is absent.**  
    Quote, SAP §3: “주분석 유지 / 민감도에서 검토: 임신부” (“retain in primary analysis; examine in sensitivity analysis”).  
    Contradiction: no named authoritative result, manuscript result, or Table S11 disposition addresses pregnancy.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: perform it or disclose that it was infeasible/not performed.

19. **The planned KCHS-only secondary model is absent.**  
    Quote, SAP §4: KCHS-only variables including perceived stress are “국내 보조 모델 및 민감도 전용.”  
    Contradiction: no authoritative result or deviation reports that secondary model.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: provide the model/sensitivity analysis or record the deviation.

20. **The prespecified recalibration sequence is incomplete.**  
    Quote, SAP §12: “① 절편만 … ② 절편+기울기 … ③ Platt/temperature scaling 비교.”  
    Contradiction: the authoritative results report intercept/slope recalibration only; intercept-only and Platt/temperature comparisons are absent and undisclosed in Table S11.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: run all stages or explicitly log their omission.

## 4. Cross-document consistency and provenance — defects found

21. **The evidence ledger cites superseded sources as current evidence.**  
    Quotes: `evidence_ledger.md` cites `audit_recompute_metrics.csv`, `gain_14to17_bootstrap.csv`, and `fairness.csv`.  
    Contradiction: `results/_SUPERSEDED.md` supersedes these with `review2_metrics.csv`/`review3_metrics.csv`, `review2_gain.csv`, and `review3_fairness_domain.csv`.  
    Severity: **important**.  
    Correction: replace every active ledger citation with the exact authoritative file and row.

22. **The model card’s reproducibility instructions select superseded files.**  
    Quote: “Current results are `results/review2_*.csv`, `review3_*.csv` … earlier result generations are retained under `results/_superseded/`.”  
